  "next_id": 75,
  "notes": [
    {
      "at": [
        -40,
        -40
      ],
      "id": 74,
      "text": "A rotary encoder (PB6/PB7, internal pull-ups) sets a position of 0-20 detents that three motors follow:\na servo on TIM2 CH1 (PA0, 9 degrees per detent), a 28BYJ-48 stepper through a ULN2003 (PB12-PB15) and a DC motor\nthrough an L298 (PB0/PB1 direction, PWM on ENA from TIM2 CH2). Run, then drag the encoder or turn the wheel over it;\nthe UART terminal reports the position. The four diodes protect the L298 from the motor's inductive kicks."
    }
  ],
